From 3ca62e7fcaa115cd9fbfc524147e07b5ddccefd8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bringup <bringup@local>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 00:41:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 32/38] kebab: XNU-003 FIX FATSz16 was never written into the
 BPB

The generated volume left BPB_FATSz16 (offset 22) at zero, so the FAT
driver could not locate the data area; UniXNU saw no unixnu.toml and fell
back to its built-in menu. The validated XNU-001b image has FATSz16=3.

Now one sector per FAT (258 entries * 1.5 bytes = 387 <= 512).
---
 .../Drivers/XnuRamDiskDxe/XnuConfigFat12.img  | Bin 524288 -> 524288 bytes
 .../Drivers/XnuRamDiskDxe/mkfat12_dir.py      |   1 +
 2 files changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/Silicon/Silicium/SiliciumPkg/Drivers/XnuRamDiskDxe/XnuConfigFat12.img b/Silicon/Silicium/SiliciumPkg/Drivers/XnuRamDiskDxe/XnuConfigFat12.img
